(`${{ values.runtime }}`), defined with Terraform.

## Layout

| Path                                 | Contents                                                        |
| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| {% if 'java' in values.runtime %}`src/`, `pom.xml`  {% else %}`src/`, `tests/`    {% endif %}                 | The Lambda function and its unit tests                          |
| `infra/`                             | Terraform configuration of the API, the function and the rest   |
| `infra/terraform.tfvars.json`        | The choices made when the repository was created                |
| `.github/actions/build-lambda/`      | Tests the function and writes `build/lambda.zip`                |
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml`           | Validation on every push and pull request                       |
{%- if values.enableCICD %}
| `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`       | Plan and apply, once AWS credentials are configured             |
{%- endif %}
{%- if values.enableAuth and values.authType == 'jwt' %}
| `authorizer/`                        | Lambda authorizer that verifies bearer tokens                   |
{%- endif %}
| `docs/`                              | Documentation shown in the portal (TechDocs)                    |
| `catalog-info.yaml`                  | Registration of the service and its API in the portal           |

## Documentation

- [Overview](docs/index.md): what was created and why
- [API](docs/api.md): endpoints, authentication, rate limits
- [Development](docs/development.md): run the tests, build the package, add an endpoint
- [Operations](docs/operations.md): deploy, monitor, change settings

## Pipeline

`ci.yml` needs no AWS account. It tests and packages the function, checks the
Terraform formatting, validates the configuration, plans it against mocked
providers, lints it, scans it with Trivy and builds the documentation.
{%- if values.enableCICD %}

`deploy.yml` plans on pull requests and applies on `main`. It skips both until
the role and state bucket described in [Operations](docs/operations.md) are
configured.
{%- endif %}
